  "notes": "Transitive ichidan verb. The subject actively puts distance between themselves (or others) and the object. Can be used for physical distance (sense 1) or social/emotional distance (sense 2).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {遠|とお}ざける (transitive): to keep something/someone away\n- {遠|とお}ざかる (intransitive): to move away, to become distant\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {危険|きけん}から{遠|とお}ざける: to keep away from danger\n- {人|ひと}を{遠|とお}ざける: to push people away\n- お{酒|さけ}を{遠|とお}ざける: to stay away from alcohol\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {避|さ}ける: to avoid — focuses on actively dodging or steering clear\n- {離|はな}す: to separate — physical separation of objects\n- {敬遠|けいえん}する: to keep at arm's length — to avoid out of respect or caution",
